BT /F2 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 585.6 Tm (1. What JUPI is) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 563.6 Tm (JUPI \(Joint Unix Platform Integrator\) is an old PlayStation 4 that runs Linux instead of games.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 552 Tm (It becomes a small, quiet science computer: it can run a local AI model \(answers stay in the room\),) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 540.4 Tm (do maths on its graphics chip, store data, and talk to other JUPIs over a cable.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 523.8 Tm (Why: these machines are e-waste. Their memory and graphics chips still work. Reusing them is) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 512.2 Tm (recycling at the scale of compute.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 495.6 Tm (How it starts, in one line: a small PS4 Linux loader \(linux-1024mb.bin\) is started on the console) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 484 Tm (and hands the machine to Linux. How that loader is delivered to the console is out of scope for this) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 472.4 Tm (repo and kept private. \(CONFIRMED, see section 4.\)) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 455.8 Tm (There are two in the rack today:) Tj T* ET
BT /F3 7.4 Tf 8.88 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 56 439.2 Tm (| Name | Console | Starts Linux | Boot stick label |) Tj T* ET
