1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 742 Tm (\(CONFIRMED\). If it hangs, a person decides.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 712.4 Tm (7. Updating JUPI \(the safe way\)) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 690.4 Tm (The rule: the launcher \(the loader\) never changes. An update only changes files on) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 678.8 Tm (the stick, from inside Linux, and every update can undo itself.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 662.2 Tm (The tool that does the undo is the TRIAL GUARD \(installed Nov 24 2026, idle, on both units; CONFIRMED\):) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 56 650.6 Tm (- /usr/local/sbin/jupi-trial-guard.sh sha256 15ea6e93b6fb6fae96a74519da752b10fd357ede12bc7e6a0dbb5497b05ef085) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 56 639 Tm (- /etc/systemd/system/jupi-trial-guard.service sha256) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 56 627.4 Tm (5fbe9332a2e963f4cb3d9d1fb7ae0ade0b0dcdb26fd6dd6a156af0f68a58fba5) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 610.8 Tm (How a kernel update goes:) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 599.2 Tm (1. Copy the new kernel to the stick with a new name, e.g. bzImage.jupi-1.0. Check its sha256.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 587.6 Tm (2. Arm one trial:) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 576 Tm (sudo jupi-trial-guard.sh arm bzImage.jupi-1.0 <new-sha> bzImage.pidfsfix-20261120 <good-sha> jupi-1.0) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 564.4 Tm (It refuses if a fingerprint is wrong.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 552.8 Tm (3. Restart JUPI the normal way.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 541.2 Tm (4. The guard checks every minute: network up, the peer answers, SSH running, no GPU hang/Oops.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 529.6 Tm (- 15 healthy minutes -> PASS. The new kernel stays.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 518 Tm (- 3 bad checks in a row -> REVERT. The old kernel is put back on the stick. Restart once more.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 62 506.4 Tm (- If the new kernel can't even start Linux: turn off, pull the stick, start \(disk backup kernel\),) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 494.8 Tm (plug the stick back in, then run sudo jupi-trial-guard.sh revert \(puts the old kernel back on) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 483.2 Tm (the stick; the guard does not watch for a re-plugged stick by itself\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 471.6 Tm (5. sudo jupi-trial-guard.sh status shows where you are. The log is /var/log/jupi-trial.log.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 455 Tm (Stop switch: sudo touch /etc/jupi-trial/DISABLE \(guard does nothing at all\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 443.4 Tm (The guard never restarts or powers off the machine \(CONFIRMED in code and in 11/11 simulated tests\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 431.8 Tm (When idle it only reads the stick \(CONFIRMED: whole-stick fingerprint identical before and after\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 415.2 Tm (Coming later: one command, sudo jupi-update <file> <sha256>, that does steps 1-2 for you) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 403.6 Tm (\(design only today; not published\).) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 387 Tm (Not used for updates: kexec \(Linux starting another Linux directly\). It is built in, but others) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 11.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 48 375.4 Tm (report it freezes on PS4 \(OBSERVED\). Untested by us.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
